{
  "id": "vivaldi",
  "name": "Vivaldi",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Browser",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "vivaldi.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.vivaldi.Vivaldi"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://help.vivaldi.com/desktop/shortcuts/keyboard-shortcuts/",
    "https://help.vivaldi.com/desktop/shortcuts/single-key-shortcuts/",
    "https://help.vivaldi.com/desktop/shortcuts/quick-commands/",
    "https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/157179"
  ],
  "note": "Vivaldi's own \"Keyboard Shortcuts\" help page does not publish a text list of the default chord shortcuts: it only points to an in-app cheat sheet reachable via Ctrl+F1 (rendered as a screenshot, not text) and Settings > Keyboard, where every shortcut is user-remappable. What IS documented in text on help.vivaldi.com is used directly: the Ctrl+F1 cheat-sheet shortcut itself, Quick Commands (F2 / Cmd+E), and the single-key shortcuts (Z / X for history back/forward, Tab, Space). Vivaldi is built on Chromium, and its Settings > Keyboard defaults for standard browser actions (new tab, close tab, navigation, zoom, find, bookmarks, devtools, etc.) match Chromium's; those entries below are taken from Google's official Chrome keyboard-shortcuts page as the documented Chromium baseline Vivaldi inherits, per the same approach used for Brave. The page's other single-key examples (tab-switching on 1-4, zoom on 6-9-0) were left out because the page does not say which digit maps to which specific action, and \"Main menu - Alt\" was left out because a bare modifier key isn't an expressible chord. Skipped as not expressible: mouse-modifier combinations (Ctrl+click, Shift+click, Alt+scroll for the Tab Cycler) documented under \"Keyboard modifiers\".",
  "actions": [
    {
      "name": "View the keyboard shortcut cheat sheet",
      "context": "",
      "windows": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Ctrl+F1"
      },
      "mac": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Cmd+F1"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Open Quick Commands",
      "context": "",
      "windows": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "F2"
      },
      "mac": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Cmd+E"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Focus on the next element on the page",
      "context": "",
      "windows": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Tab"
      },
      "mac": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Tab"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Fast forward to the next page (paginated content)",
      "context": "",
      "windows": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Space"
      },
      "mac": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Space"
      }
    },
    {
